  "text": "Argentina lost control because they stopped threatening France consistently, then Mbappé turned growing pressure into a sudden comeback. Early in that spell, France had 66% of the completed passes, while Argentina produced no shots. Kolo Muani’s attempt shows France were already finding openings before the later substitutions. [[ev:sb:3869685:2517]]\n\nComan and Camavinga’s introductions gave France fresh options, but the evidence does not show uninterrupted domination afterward. Argentina recovered more of the ball without creating much danger, and Otamendi’s incomplete clearance under pressure illustrated their difficulty escaping cleanly. [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[seq:sb:3869685:s157]] The decisive change came around Mbappé’s penalty and Thuram’s pass for his equaliser: France’s share of attacking territory rose from 42% before that turning point to 72% afterward. In short, Argentina’s possession stopped providing either an attacking outlet or defensive security. [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[seq:sb:3869685:s165]]",
